class.description:
[TextDataFormat] holds the parsed [member data] of one text file. It is the abstract base of [INI], [CSV], [XML], [TOML] and [YAML] and of formats added by modules or extensions; use one of those classes. Like [JSON], these classes are [Resource]s: [code]load("res://x.ini")[/code] of a plain file returns the format resource, while files with a [code]$type[/code] marker load as the serialized resource. Plain files load with the project default options.
[TextDataFormat] is the text document of a data file, nothing else: [method parse] with the kept text, the error with line and column, [member options], [method load] and [method save], [method validate] and the file extensions. It holds no data model shared by the formats. Each format class gives [member data] its own type ([CSV]: [Array] of rows, [INI], [XML] and [TOML]: [Dictionary], [YAML]: any value) and has its own API to read and edit it, such as [method CSV.get_cell], [method INI.set_value], [method XML.get_root], [method TOML.get_value] or [method YAML.get_value]. The loaders, the text editor and the serializer treat all formats alike through this class; the editor has an inspector per format, and docks by use: the INI dock, the Localization Table for translation CSVs and the Dataset dock shared by every format with a table. [JSON] is not a [TextDataFormat], but works the same way.
[method parse] reads text into [member data]. With [code]keep_text[/code], the text is kept (also if it has errors, like [member JSON.data] after [method JSON.parse]) and written back as it is on save while [member data] is unchanged, so comments and formatting survive. The editor keeps the text of files it opens; exported games do not, to save memory.
The instance methods [method load] and [method save] work like [method ConfigFile.load] and [method ConfigFile.save]: they do not use the resource cache and do not set [member Resource.resource_path]. In exported games [code]res://[/code] is read-only, so save to [code]user://[/code].
Changing the data (in the inspector, by setting [member data], or with the editing methods of the subclasses such as [method INI.set_value], [method CSV.set_cell] or the writes of [XMLElement]) drops the kept text, so comments and formatting are lost on the next save.
[member options] decides how text is read and written ([member SerializerOptions.csv_delimiter], [member SerializerOptions.indent], ...). [code]null[/code] uses the project settings.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var file = TOML.new()
if file.parse("# Window\n[window]\nwidth = 1280\n", true) == OK:
	print(file.data["window"]["width"]) # Prints 1280
	file.save("user://window.toml") # Saved as parsed, with the comment.
else:
	print("Line %d, column %d: %s" % [file.get_error_line(), file.get_error_column(), file.get_error_message()])
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var file = new Toml();
if (file.Parse("# Window\n[window]\nwidth = 1280\n", true) == Error.Ok)
{
	GD.Print(file.Data.AsGodotDictionary()["window"].AsGodotDictionary()["width"]); // Prints 1280
	file.Save("user://window.toml"); // Saved as parsed, with the comment.
}
else
{
	GD.Print($"Line {file.GetErrorLine()}, column {file.GetErrorColumn()}: {file.GetErrorMessage()}");
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] An instance should be used by one thread at a time.

method.description:
Validates [member data] against [param schema] and returns the issues (see [method DataSchema.validate]). If the last [method parse] failed, the result holds one [constant DataValidation.ISSUE_KIND_PARSE_ERROR] with the line of [method get_error_line].
With [member DataValidationOptions.keep_positions] and the text kept by [method parse] (the editor keeps it), every issue gets its 1-based line: exact for [CSV] rows (also with quoted cells over several lines), searched by the keys of the issue path for the other formats.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var items = CSV.new()
items.parse(FileAccess.get_file_as_string("res://data/items.csv"))
var result = items.validate(load("res://data/items_schema.tres"))
for i in result.get_issue_count():
	print("Row %d: %s" % [result.get_issue_row(i), result.get_issue_message(i)])
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var items = new Csv();
items.Parse(FileAccess.GetFileAsString("res://data/items.csv"));
DataValidation result = items.Validate(GD.Load<DataSchema>("res://data/items_schema.tres"));
for (int i = 0; i < result.GetIssueCount(); i++)
{
	GD.Print($"Row {result.GetIssueRow(i)}: {result.GetIssueMessage(i)}");
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
Validation is never done on load or when [member data] changes; call this method when needed.
